  "result": "The fix is in. The type check passes and the full suite passes (73 files, 617 tests). I also ran two temporary checks, one covering the paging and deleted-workspace cases and one covering the migration on an old database, and deleted them afterwards.\n\nChoices I made:\n- **Cleanup also covers deleted workspaces.** Today it processes them, and retention should still apply to their content. The spec only excluded deleted workspaces from overdue alerts and the digest.\n- **New `recounted_at` column on `organization_usage`.** Only a full recount sets it, and the rollup queue sorts on it. `measured_at` still moves on every counter delta, which is why it couldn't serve as the queue key. The column is added to the schema, to the `migrate.ts` fallback, and to existing databases by a guarded `ALTER`.\n\nNot changed: the cleanup job only inspects the first 100 issues per workspace (`PAGE_SIZE`), so archived issues beyond that page are never purged. That is a separate bug from the one you reported.",
